---
description: BusinessOS engineering constitution
alwaysApply: true
---

Work incrementally in this repository. Do not rebuild BusinessOS. Do not delete working POS, inventory, sales, auth, or reporting.

Never trust the browser for prices, stock, discounts, payment confirmation, or permissions. Validate on the server and in Postgres.

Use migrations for schema changes. Do not drop tables, disable RLS, or reset production data.

Online orders stay off the sales ledger until a merchant records payment. Do not call `create_sale` from public checkout.

Platform Paynow is subscription billing only. Do not use those keys for customer shop funds.

Do not invent verification badges, reviews, stock, legal compliance, or sent notifications.

Do not put secrets in client code. Keep tenant data isolated.

UI copy: no em dashes. Prefer complete vertical slices over unfinished decorative screens.

Staging is the only default migration target. Production requires explicit human approval.
